                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8e219efd-cbaf-386d-bb2b-65b0eaf5b85c",
                        "entry_id": "e6479ad0-37f3-3429-b6fd-4b20f7723ba1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "быть живым и здоровым, находиться в хорошем состоянии, благополучно существовать"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8eafc8e3-c58f-4490-a1ba-06320106ef47",
                                "sense_id": "8e219efd-cbaf-386d-bb2b-65b0eaf5b85c",
                                "text": "Николай Иванович, слава богу, живёт и здравствует."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "72d6baae-949d-3b31-9f7c-93f6285e3f6e",
                        "entry_id": "e6479ad0-37f3-3429-b6fd-4b20f7723ba1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "повел. обычная формула вежливого приветствия"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed3ac56e-9682-4db7-9935-d82e6930960f",
                                "sense_id": "72d6baae-949d-3b31-9f7c-93f6285e3f6e",
                                "text": "Здравствуйте, Виктор Степанович!"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3a2a3771-970c-4900-9c56-501de36f008d",
                        "source_entry_id": "e6479ad0-37f3-3429-b6fd-4b20f7723ba1",
                        "target_lang_word": "be well",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e30748f0-363c-4e37-b09f-18194311c989",
                        "source_entry_id": "e6479ad0-37f3-3429-b6fd-4b20f7723ba1",
                        "target_lang_word": "prosper",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "prosper",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "99990140-eeb0-374f-99b6-2a6dfcb6c31d",
                                        "entry_id": "88a82597-9cbc-3bb0-90a9-e0a243e816ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be successful; to succeed; to be fortunate or prosperous; to thrive; to make gain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a022937-6d62-4953-a050-ce0b85f4902c",
                                                "sense_id": "99990140-eeb0-374f-99b6-2a6dfcb6c31d",
                                                "text": "Yet his passion for her had grown fiercer than ever, and he swore to himself that he would win her back from her phantasies. She, one may believe, was ready enough to listen. As she walked with him by the Sker water his words were like musick to her ears, and Alison within doors laughed to herself and saw her devices prosper."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d16f3ac5-5b88-3200-8489-ca3ebdd435a7",
                                        "entry_id": "88a82597-9cbc-3bb0-90a9-e0a243e816ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To grow; to increase."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25544ad6-6ec2-4345-a37e-63f98718791a",
                                                "sense_id": "d16f3ac5-5b88-3200-8489-ca3ebdd435a7",
                                                "text": "And his master saw that the Lord was with him, and that the Lord made all that he did to prosper in his hand."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e68390b7-285b-3888-a02f-52d1406fdcc2",
                                        "entry_id": "88a82597-9cbc-3bb0-90a9-e0a243e816ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To favor; to render successful."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e33ef26-ad6e-4112-9927-a0fdfd6e370a",
                                                "sense_id": "e68390b7-285b-3888-a02f-52d1406fdcc2",
                                                "text": "Prosper thou our handiwork."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "67ec469f-fc1c-4956-89e5-629097a50ee1",
                                                "sense_id": "e68390b7-285b-3888-a02f-52d1406fdcc2",
                                                "text": "The Gods defenders of the innocent,\nWill neuer proſper your intended driftes,\nThat thus oppreſſe poore friendles paſſengers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9816c26e-0e2e-4008-8c4b-ff9e7318e311",
                                                "sense_id": "e68390b7-285b-3888-a02f-52d1406fdcc2",
                                                "text": "All things concur to prosper our design."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fc1d3e75-7b63-4bfc-897b-63d80c9a8044",
                        "source_entry_id": "e6479ad0-37f3-3429-b6fd-4b20f7723ba1",
                        "target_lang_word": "thrive",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "thrive",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "61002621-d253-3a5e-9935-e6c4cc5e187c",
                                        "entry_id": "cb3e133b-0618-3ca0-a719-e2e7015c778a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To grow or increase stature; to grow vigorously or luxuriantly, to flourish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c00fe924-320d-4383-acb9-d6f723d53b32",
                                                "sense_id": "61002621-d253-3a5e-9935-e6c4cc5e187c",
                                                "text": "Not all animals thrive well in captivity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3259206e-ec6a-4779-8d28-cda395d0224d",
                                                "sense_id": "61002621-d253-3a5e-9935-e6c4cc5e187c",
                                                "text": "to thrive upon hard work"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "536bf922-10e5-436a-8663-6a4548bef236",
                                                "sense_id": "61002621-d253-3a5e-9935-e6c4cc5e187c",
                                                "text": "“It seems to me, reverend father,” said the knight, “that the small morsels which you eat, together with this holy, but somewhat thin beverage, have thriven with you marvellously.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "baf63edb-04a9-4a71-a96e-38aea0fe37bf",
                                                "sense_id": "61002621-d253-3a5e-9935-e6c4cc5e187c",
                                                "text": "So, on I went. I think I never saw / Such starved ignoble nature; nothing throve: / For flowers - as well expect a cedar grove!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8838126-f961-4ed6-9bb4-a83111e3a5af",
                                                "sense_id": "61002621-d253-3a5e-9935-e6c4cc5e187c",
                                                "text": "Dwarves had not passed that way for many years, but Gandalf had, and he knew how evil and danger had grown and thriven in the Wild, since the dragons had driven men from the lands, and the goblins had spread in secret after the battle of the Mines of Moria."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc656738-bcd9-4e8e-8793-fa0cb9ce9fb6",
                                                "sense_id": "61002621-d253-3a5e-9935-e6c4cc5e187c",
                                                "text": "The growing things jumbled themselves together into a dense thicket; so tensely earnest were things about growing in Skedans that everything linked with everything else, hurrying to grow to the limit of its own capacity; weeds and weaklings alike throve in the rich moistness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a160dd4-8dd6-4964-93e3-bc987084eaf6",
                                                "sense_id": "61002621-d253-3a5e-9935-e6c4cc5e187c",
                                                "text": "Despite a thriving global computer security industry that is projected to reach $79 billion in revenues next year, and the fact that in 2002 Microsoft itself began an intense corporatewide effort to improve the security of its software, Internet security has continued to deteriorate globally."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1e0d08be-ded8-351b-924e-efcaab53f320",
                                        "entry_id": "cb3e133b-0618-3ca0-a719-e2e7015c778a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To increase in wealth or success; to prosper, be profitable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73c78d4f-2048-499e-8855-6aea6dad26cf",
                                                "sense_id": "1e0d08be-ded8-351b-924e-efcaab53f320",
                                                "text": "Since expanding in June, the business has really thrived."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de10d605-c747-465e-9b56-5c893452b584",
                                                "sense_id": "1e0d08be-ded8-351b-924e-efcaab53f320",
                                                "text": "[…] Deliver me the key.\nHere do I choose, and thrive I as I may!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f2f3908-c6ac-4c6a-b051-dd9d4a6c5d18",
                                                "sense_id": "1e0d08be-ded8-351b-924e-efcaab53f320",
                                                "text": "On the Chickahominy, the Hazelwood brothers' fish house at Hicks Island and the Menzel brothers' fish house near the old shipyard thrived by serving local and distant markets. As late as 1977, a Publick Observer article boasted, \"If you are served turtle soup in Atlanta or catfish in Ft. Wayne, Ind., chances are good that the main ingredients came from the waters of the James or the Chickahominy.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da7f6dfb-a186-44ba-8593-ab282d5b16a3",
                                                "sense_id": "1e0d08be-ded8-351b-924e-efcaab53f320",
                                                "text": "Though they obviously realized that these episodes were part of something wonderful and important and lasting, the writers and producers couldn’t have imagined that 20 years later “Treehouse Of Horror” wouldn’t just survive; it’d thrive as one of the most talked-about and watched episodes of every season of The Simpsons."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68d914b2-1206-460d-ae9d-e0ca3b672ebc",
                                                "sense_id": "1e0d08be-ded8-351b-924e-efcaab53f320",
                                                "text": "And, reader, the further you take this analogy the more beautifully it works: my anxiety disorder thrives on irrational scaremongery and paranoia, it often demands booze (but should not be given alcohol because it only makes it worse) and just when you think you have got rid of it for good, it pops up again."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
